Given an array and a number T, find the minimum absolute difference between T and sum of any subarray.
Ex: input: 4 a[1 2 3 4] 6 output: 0 Explanation: We check all possible subarrays and calculate their sums. Subarray [1, 2, 3] gives sum = 6, which exactly matches target T = 6. So, minimum difference = |6 - 6| = 0 (perfect match).

Input Format
First line: Integer N Second line: Array elements Third line: Integer T
Constraints
1 ≤ N ≤ 1000
Output Format
Print minimum difference
Sample Input 0
4
1 2 3 4
6
Sample Output 0
0
Sample Input 1
5
1 1 1 1 1
3
Sample Output 1
0
//code
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <math.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
int n;
    scanf("%d",&n);
    int arr[n];
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        scanf("%d",&arr[i]);
    }
    int T;
    scanf("%d",&T);
    int min_diff=10000;
   
    int diff;
    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
         int sum=0;
        for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
            sum +=arr[j];
            diff=abs(T-sum);
            if(diff<min_diff){
                min_diff=diff;
            }
        }
    }
    printf("%d",min_diff);
    return 0;
}

